WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.729
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:12.729 --> 00:00:19.028
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:19.028 --> 00:00:35.028
Liar’s Deck: be the last survivor
Each survivor receives 5 cards and the table announces a target face. Follow Demo E; opponents’ face-down cards and bullet positions stay hidden.

00:00:35.028 --> 00:00:46.028
Select one to three cards and Play
Click one to three of your cards, then press Play. They go face down with a claim that every card matches the target face.

00:00:46.028 --> 00:00:55.028
Target cards and jokers are truthful. Other cards can be bluffs. You know only your own hand and your own played cards.

00:00:55.028 --> 00:01:07.128
Press LIAR to challenge the last play
A face-down play is on the table. The next player may play or press LIAR to reveal it; its truth is unknown before that reveal.

00:01:07.128 --> 00:01:17.028
Only the challenged play is exposed. Any false card makes its player pull the trigger; a completely honest play makes the challenger pull.

00:01:17.028 --> 00:01:28.028
Judge only after the public reveal
The first play revealed a joker and was honest. The challenger pulled once and survived. Fresh hands and a new target face have now appeared.

00:01:28.028 --> 00:01:37.028
Each six-chamber revolver has one fixed bullet for the match. Pull counts are public. Surviving once does not make the next pull safe.

00:01:37.028 --> 00:01:55.028
Judge the next round for yourself
Continue with face-down claims and challenges. Confirm who lied and who must pull only after the public reveal appears in the log.

00:01:55.028 --> 00:02:07.128
Elimination and the next starter
This challenge exposed a false ace. Its player pulled again and survived. Continue to the next public outcome.

00:02:07.128 --> 00:02:17.028
A surviving shooter starts the next round. A killed shooter passes that role to the next survivor; eliminated players cannot act.

00:02:17.028 --> 00:02:28.028
Sometimes a challenge is compulsory
Demo W has now been eliminated by a public shot outcome. The survivors continue, with other hands still shown as counts only.

00:02:28.028 --> 00:02:37.027
A fresh round opens with a play. Later turns may challenge the preceding play. The last player holding cards must call LIAR. Emptying a hand does not win the match.

00:02:37.027 --> 00:03:07.027
Speed through to the last survivor
All remaining claims, challenges, reveals, and trigger pulls play in order at higher speed. Outcomes appear only when publicly resolved.

00:03:07.027 --> 00:03:26.034
Liar’s Deck: final survival order
Demo E is the last survivor. Demo W, N, and S were eliminated in that order across eight rounds.
